**RENOVATION LOAN AGREEMENT**

THIS AGREEMENT is made this ______ day of ________, 20______, by and between ABC Construction Ltd., a company incorporated under the laws of England and Wales, with its registered office at 1234 Fifth Avenue, London W1T 1NB (hereinafter referred to as the "Borrower"), and XYZ Bank Plc., a public limited company incorporated under the laws of England and Wales, with its registered office at 5678 Ninth Street, London E1W 2AB (hereinafter referred to as the "Lender").

WHEREAS, the Borrower desires to borrow from the Lender a certain sum of money for the purpose of financing the renovation of its commercial property situated at 1234 Fifth Avenue, London W1T 1NB (hereinafter referred to as the "Property");

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the premises and the mutual covenants contained herein and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged, the parties agree as follows:

1. **LOAN AMOUNT AND DISBURSEMENT**

The Lender shall disburse the loan proceeds to the Borrower in accordance with the following milestones:

a. Upon execution of this Agreement, the Lender shall disburse an amount of £50,000 to the Borrower for the initial renovation costs (the "Initial Disbursement");

b. Upon completion of 50% of the renovation work, the Borrower shall provide the Lender with a written certification from a licensed architect or engineer, confirming such completion. Upon receipt of such certification, the Lender shall disburse an amount of £75,000 to the Borrower (the "First Progress Disbursement");

c. Upon completion of 100% of the renovation work, the Borrower shall provide the Lender with a final written certification from a licensed architect or engineer, confirming such completion. Upon receipt of such certification, the Lender shall disburse an amount of £100,000 to the Borrower (the "Final Disbursement").

