BUY-SELL AGREEMENT

THIS AGREEMENT is made this ______ day of ________, 20_____, by and between ___________ Limited (the "Company"), and Agapito M. Ferrando, a natural person with a residential address at 6 Hartley Green (the "Shareholder").

RECITALS

WHEREAS, the Shareholder is the legal owner of __________ shares of the Company's common stock, with the employee ID G-649126-Z; and

WHEREAS, the Company and the Shareholder wish to establish a fair and equitable procedure for the purchase and sale of the Shares in the event of certain triggering events;

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and promises contained herein and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged, the parties hereto agree as follows:

1. TRIGGERING EVENTS. The purchase and sale of the Shares shall be automatically triggered upon the occurrence of any of the following events (each, a "Triggering Event"):

(a) The death or Disability of the Shareholder;

(b) The termination of the Shareholder's employment or service with the Company for any reason;

(c) The Shareholder's retirement from the Company;

(d) The Shareholder's voluntary transfer of the Shares to any third party;

(e) The Shareholder's bankruptcy or insolvency;

(f) The occurrence of any event that would reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect on the business, operations, or financial condition of the Company; or

(g) Any other event or circumstance that the Company and the Shareholder agree in writing shall constitute a Triggering Event.

2. PURCHASE PRICE. Upon the occurrence of a Triggering Event, the Company shall have the option, but not the obligation, to purchase all of the Shares from the Shareholder or the Shareholder's estate or legal representative, as the case may be, for a purchase price equal to the fair market value of the Shares as of the date of the Triggering Event, as determined by a mutually agreed upon appraiser.

